What it does show is that the thesis pipeline remains operational when the
regular toy grid is replaced by a real urban street topology: the scenario
generator produces routable demand, the plan representation remains valid,
Monte Carlo route variation is reproducible over 30 runs and the evaluator
returns an interpretable recommendation with an explicit trade-off rather than
a purely visual judgement.

\subsection{Closure of the Delta tunnel}

The Flagey experiment establishes that the pipeline survives a real street
topology. The Delta experiment asks a harder question: whether it can answer an
\emph{operationally posed} question, of the kind a road authority actually
formulates when it schedules maintenance. The study area is the Delta
interchange in Auderghem, where the E411 enters Brussels and the closure is the
Delta tunnel between 23:00 and 06:00. \cite{rtbf_delta_2024}. This is precisely the class of decision the present framework is meant to
support: a planned, announced closure of a known structure, for which several
diversion itineraries exist and must be chosen between and signal timings
adjusted, all of it before the first vehicle is affected.

\subsubsection{Experimental setup}

The network was extracted from OpenStreetMap and filtered to passenger-car
roads before conversion to SUMO. It contains 310 directed non-internal road
edges, 371 lanes, 163 non-internal junctions and 32.52 lane-kilometres. A
